99. In Shorter Oxford English Dictionary, (5 th ed, 2003, Volume 2) the meaning of the word "such" is defined as "of the kind, degree, or category previously specified or implied contextually; of the same kind or degree as something previously specific or implied contextually; of that kind; similar; of the character previously specified by a preceding adjective, so;
of the kind, degree, category being or about to be specified."
100.
